      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hi, here's some tips to avoid a public avatar from being found:\n\n1. Avoid wearing the avatar around any users (including potentially yourself) with third-party API spyware clients (for example, VRCX). In particular, VRCX has a submission feature to avatar databases for public avatars.\n\n2. Avoid \"Loading...\" and some other suspicious titles in the avatar name or description.\n\n3. Make sure the avatar has not been recently updated. These recently updated avatars show up up and front on avatar indexers!\n\n4. Avoid using a recognizable, \"meme-y\" or blank avatar name and picture which may stick out like a sore eye from other avatars.\n\n5. Avoid Public/Group Public instances (hotspots).\n\n6. If feasible, avoid the \"Very Poor\" performance ranking.\n\nThis does not still permit uploading content that violates the [Creator Guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/creator-guidelines) and such.",
